.next
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
# This repo intentionally commits node_modules (so cloning it is enough —
# no install step needed to rebuild). .next and the export output below are
# still regenerated on every build, so there's nothing worth tracking there.
# `next build`'s static-export output. Not committed — .github/workflows/
# pages.yml builds it fresh and publishes it to GitHub Pages on every push.
/out
# Regenerated by scripts/copy-vendor.mjs's postinstall hook on every install
# (ffmpeg.wasm's ~10 MB core, gzipped and split) — never hand-edited, and
# nothing on the pages that remain in this static export actually uses it.
public/vendor/ffmpeg-core/
# The one piece of node_modules NOT committed, despite the rest of it being
# tracked above: GitHub hard-rejects any single git object over 100 MB, and
# this native binary (Next's Rust-based compiler, @next/swc) is ~125 MB on
# this platform. Git LFS is the normal fix, but this repo was pushed from an
# environment whose network policy couldn't reach LFS's storage backend —
# see .github/workflows/pages.yml, which fetches just this one package
# before building, since GitHub's own runners have no such restriction.
node_modules/.pnpm/@next+swc-linux-x64-gnu@*/node_modules/@next/swc-linux-x64-gnu/*.node
